tickets/in-progress/agent-team-hierarchical-handoffs/design-spec.md:169:4. When `20260517...` is pending, it uses that decoder, validates the complete staged predecessor through the corrected canonical converter, then backs up and atomically replaces flat input with predecessor `memberTree`. In `20260801...`, accept already-current v3, predecessor `memberTree`, or residual flat v1. A residual flat file is decoded to predecessor form in memory with the exact same decoder, then proceeds through the canonical converter without an intermediate write. For each predecessor node, normalize separators/trim, require `memberRouteKey === memberPath.join("/")`, require exact recursive parent/direct-child structure and unique canonical addresses, and derive `AgentTeamAddress` from that agreed structural pair. Require `memberName` only as valid historical display input; never compare it with the route/path basename and never use it as fallback. The v3 target intentionally omits it.
